  "construction": "Regular {7,7} hyperbolic surface code on a closed orientable surface. Quotient Q = Delta_7/Gamma with Q = PSL(2,7); the face-vertex swap is a projective involution J in PGL(2,7) imposing y = J x J^-1, with ord(x) = ord(y) = 7 and ord(xy) = 2. Data qubits on edges = left cosets of the order-2 subgroup <xy>; Z checks on face boundaries = left cosets of <x>; X checks on vertex stars = left cosets of <y>. Checks commute because each face boundary meets each vertex an even number of times. n = |Q|/2 and k/n = (7-4)/7 + 2/n by Euler, giving k=38 at n=84. Regenerated from the algebra of arXiv:2610.10948 Sec. II by research/hyperbolic_psl.py; the matrices are recomputed, not copied, since that paper publishes its matrices on request only.",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2610.10948"
  ],
  "date": "2026-10-10",
  "notes": "Distance is a homological systole: a shortest cycle in the primal graph outside the GF(2) span of the face boundaries is a genuine logical. Both the X and Z operators here are weight 3 and are carried as explicit witnesses, so d<=3 is witness-backed, not certified exact.",
